# The kernel: Linux LTS built for real machines as well as QEMU. What is
# needed to reach the root filesystem and a picture is built in (NVMe, AHCI,
# USB storage, SD, virtio, ext4, vfat, simpledrm), so there is no initramfs;
# the rest (GPUs, Wi-Fi, Ethernet, sound, laptop drivers) is modules in
# /usr/lib/modules/<release>, loaded by palm-modules. Built by
# distro/kernel/build.sh; distro/notes/kernel.md is the reference.
#
# The kernel is installed twice. /boot/vmlinuz is the root's copy (the live
# ISO and the installer take it from there). /boot/efi/vmlinuz is the one
# limine boots: with the EFI system partition mounted at /boot/efi it lands
# on that partition as /vmlinuz, which limine.conf names as boot():/vmlinuz.
# palm has no hooks, so this second file is how `palm upgrade linux` reaches
# the boot loader at all.
pkgname  = linux
pkgver   = 6.18.56
pkgrel   = 1
pkgdesc  = The Linux kernel and its modules, Palmy configuration
license  = GPL-2.0-only
url      = https://kernel.org
category = System
icon     = server
details  = Linux 6.18 LTS, configured for Palmy on real hardware and in QEMU: storage, ext4, vfat and the firmware framebuffer are built in, so the system boots with no initramfs; graphics (amdgpu, i915, xe, nouveau), Wi-Fi, Ethernet, sound and laptop drivers are modules, loaded at boot for the devices the machine has.
details  = Upgrading it replaces /boot/efi/vmlinuz on the EFI system partition, which is what limine boots, so the new kernel runs after a restart. Most devices also need their firmware: install linux-firmware, or only the part for your hardware (linux-firmware-intel, linux-firmware-amdgpu, ...).
provides = cmd:palm-modules

file     = ${PALMY_OUT}/bzImage -> /boot/vmlinuz mode 0644
file     = ${PALMY_OUT}/bzImage -> /boot/efi/vmlinuz mode 0700
file     = ${PALMY_OUT}/kernel.config -> /boot/config mode 0644
tree     = ${PALMY_OUT}/modules -> /usr/lib/modules
file     = ${PALMY_OUT}/bin/palm-modules -> /usr/bin/palm-modules mode 0755
symlink  = /usr/bin/modprobe -> palm-modules
file     = ${PALMY_ROOT}/distro/kernel/10-modules -> /usr/lib/palm-init/early.d/10-modules mode 0755
